  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "When evaluating **branded residences** for a hotel project in the **Caribbean and Latin America**, an owner should first look at the hotel brands that are already most active and credible in the region: **Four Seasons, Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis, Marriott, Hilton, Hyatt/Andaz, Six Senses, Mandarin Oriental, Aman, Rosewood, and Accor’s luxury flags such as Fairmont, Raffles, and MGallery/Mondrian**.[1][2][4][6][10][12][13][16][17]\n\nThe strongest “short list” for the region is typically:\n\n- **Four Seasons** — repeatedly cited as a dominant branded-residences operator globally and in the Caribbean.[1][10][12][13]\n- **Ritz-Carlton / Ritz-Carlton Reserve** — among the top hotel-branded residence platforms globally and active in Caribbean/Latin America projects.[5][12][18]\n- **St. Regis** — a leading luxury residence brand in the Americas market.[11][12]\n- **Marriott luxury brands** — especially **JW Marriott, The Luxury Collection, and Marriott-branded residences**, given Marriott’s strong regional development activity.[6][8][17][18]\n- **Hilton luxury brands** — especially **Waldorf Astoria** and **LXR**, with Hilton explicitly expanding branded residential offerings in the region.[4][7][14]\n- **Hyatt brands** — especially **Andaz** and **Park Hyatt**, which appear in Caribbean branded-residence discussions and pipelines.[2][5][10]\n- **Six Senses** — increasingly visible in Caribbean luxury residential resort concepts.[1][2][13]\n- **Mandarin Oriental** — important for ultra-luxury positioning, even when projects are fewer in number.[1][2][5][13]\n- **Aman** — a strong ultra-luxury benchmark and relevant for the highest-end resort residences.[5][10][13]\n- **Rosewood** — a frequent competitor in luxury branded residences and part of the active new-supply set.[12][13]\n- **Accor luxury brands** — especially **Fairmont, Raffles, Banyan Tree, SLS, and Mondrian**, which expand the brand universe beyond the traditional U.S. hotel groups.[16][12]\n\nFor a practical owner’s screening, the best brands are usually those with:\n- a **proven branded-residences track record**,\n- a **specialist residential team**,\n- and the ability to provide **sales/marketing support and access to a buyer network**.[15]\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a **developer shortlist by positioning**—for example, **ultra-luxury**, **upper-upscale**, or **mixed resort/residential**—for the Caribbean and Latin America.",
